{title: Steadfast Love}
{subtitle: Psalms 130:7}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Dm7] | [Ebmaj7] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Deep down my soul is [Dm7]calling out
[Gm]To you who sit above the [Ebmaj7]clouds
[Bb]My heart is waiting on [Dm7]your word
In [Ebmaj7]all the dark and heavy fu[F7sus4]ror
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
With the [Bb]Lord there is stead[Dm7]fast love
And a[Gm]bundant redemption [Ebmaj7]flows
He will re[Bb]deem us [F/A]from our [Gm]sins
This [Cm7]is where [F7sus4]the mercy [Bb]ends
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I put my hope in what [Dm7]you say
[Gm]My soul waits more than watchmen [Ebmaj7]stay
[Bb]They wait for morning break[Dm7]ing light
I [Ebmaj7]wait for you through day and [F7sus4]night
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Forgiveness rests within your [Bb]hands
[Eb]So we may fear you as [Gm]we stand
[Eb]Not in dread but holy [Gm]awe
Your truth will [Cm7]never fail or [F7sus4]waver
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Israel, hope [Dm]in the Lord
With [Eb]him is love, a [F7sus4]living word
{end_of_verse}
